---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use - Balm"
  description="Terms of Use for Balm, a native Jira Cloud client."
>
  <main class="prose wrap">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="effective">Last updated: 17 July 2026</p>

    <h2>Acceptance</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms of Use apply to your use of the Balm macOS and iOS app and
      website. By installing or using Balm you agree to these terms. If you
      don't agree, don't use the app.
    </p>

    <h2>Apple standard EULA</h2>
    <p>
      For copies of Balm distributed through the App Store, Balm uses Apple's
      standard End User License Agreement (EULA). You can review it at <a
        href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/"
        >apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>What Balm is</h2>
    <p>
      Balm is a native client for Jira Cloud. It requires your own Atlassian
      account, and everything you do through Balm is subject to <a
        href="https://www.atlassian.com/legal">Atlassian's own terms</a
      > - Balm doesn't change what your account is allowed to do, it only gives you
      a faster way to do it.
    </p>

    <h2>No affiliation</h2>
    <p>
      Balm is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
      supported by Atlassian. Jira and the Atlassian marks are trademarks of
      Atlassian Pty Ltd.
    </p>

    <h2>Accounts and your content</h2>
    <p>
      You are responsible for keeping your Atlassian account secure and for the
      Jira issues, comments, attachments, projects, filters, notifications, and
      other content you access, create, or change through Balm. Do not upload,
      enter, or share content that you do not have the right to use.
    </p>

    <h2>Free and paid access</h2>
    <p>
      Balm may offer free and paid access depending on platform, distribution
      channel, or app version. Pricing, duration, and included features for any
      paid app purchase, subscription, or upgrade will be shown before purchase
      and confirmed by the applicable store or purchase sheet.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Payment, renewal, cancellation, refunds, and purchase management are
        handled by the store or payment provider used for that purchase.
      </li>
      <li>
        If a subscription is offered, it renews automatically unless canceled
        before the end of the current period according to the provider's rules.
      </li>
      <li>
        Canceling a subscription stops future renewal; it does not remove access
        already paid for during the current period.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Do not misuse Balm, interfere with its operation, attempt unauthorized
      access, reverse engineer protected service components, or use Balm to
      violate laws or the rights of others.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Balm uses third-party services including Atlassian for Jira Cloud
      authentication and Jira data, Apple services for App Store distribution
      and purchases where applicable, and GitHub for public support and issue
      tracking. Your use of those services may also be governed by their own
      terms and policies.
    </p>

    <h2>As is</h2>
    <p>
      Balm is provided <strong>as is</strong>, without warranty of any kind,
      express or implied - including fitness for a particular purpose and
      non-infringement. To the maximum extent permitted by law, the developer is
      not liable for any damages arising from your use of the app, including
      loss of data in your Jira instance. Actions Balm performs (creating,
      editing, transitioning, commenting) are actions <em>you</em> take with your
      account; review them as you would in any Jira client.
    </p>

    <h2>Service changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may change, suspend, or discontinue features as the app evolves. We
      will not intentionally remove paid access during a paid subscription
      period except where required for security, legal, platform compliance, or
      third-party service reasons.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may change as the app evolves; the current version is always
      posted here with its effective date. Continuing to use Balm after a change
      means you accept the new terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms? See <a href="/support">support</a>.</p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
